<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="fr">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Hors ligne — {{ site_name }}</title>
    {# Deliberately NOT extending base.html.twig: that template pulls in
       per-request dynamic globals (menus, current_user_*, config_mode,
       cookie_consent_given) built from the DB/session at render time —
       this page is precached once by the service worker and can be
       served back much later with no network at all, so nothing dynamic
       or personal must ever end up baked into that cached snapshot. Only
       already-precached assets are linked (app.css, Bootstrap Icons —
       see APP_SHELL_BASE_URLS in public/sw.js), and offline-page.js is a
       plain external script: no inline handler, no CSP nonce, since a
       nonce baked into a precached response would go stale the moment
       the server issues a new one on the next request. #}
    {# Bootstrap 5.3 themes entirely off `data-bs-theme` on the root
       element, and nothing here sets it: this page rendered in light mode for every
       dark-mode reader, which — reached from an installed app in the
       dark — is a white flash where the app used to be.

       base.html.twig gets the attribute from a tiny inline nonce'd
       script in its own head; that is exactly what this page cannot have
       (see above). So theme.js itself is loaded here instead, from the
       head and render-blocking, applying the preference before the first paint
       rather than after it. It is already in the service worker's app
       shell (APP_SHELL_BASE_URLS in public/sw.js), so it is there
       offline, which is the only state this page is ever seen in. #}
    <script src="{{ asset('/assets/js/theme.js') }}"></script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/vendor/bootstrap/css/bootstrap.min.css') }}">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/vendor/bootstrap-icons/bootstrap-icons.min.css') }}">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/app.css') }}">
</head>
{# The number of days is the `offline_cache_staleness_days` setting (#883):
   a copy older than that is never served (cachedCopy() in public/sw.js).
   A site-wide setting, not anything personal, so it may be baked into this
   precached page; it follows the version cached, which is the version
   whose service worker applies it. #}
{% set staleness_days = offline_cache_staleness_days|default(30) %}
<body data-staleness-days="{{ staleness_days }}">
    <div class="d-flex flex-column align-items-center justify-content-center text-center" style="min-height:100vh; padding:2rem;">
        <i class="bi bi-wifi-off" style="font-size:3rem;" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <h1 class="h4 mt-3">Pas de connexion</h1>
        <p class="text-body-secondary">
            Cette page n'est pas disponible hors ligne. Vérifiez votre connexion puis réessayez.
        </p>
        {# Why a page is or is not available (#883): the maintainer looked
           for a long time before finding that functional cookies were off.
           No link to the cookie preferences — that page is not available
           offline either — only where to find them once back online. #}
        <p class="text-body-secondary small" id="offline-conditions" style="max-width:32rem;">
            Une page n'est disponible hors ligne que si les cookies fonctionnels sont activés
            (depuis le pied de page, en ligne) et si vous l'avez ouverte dans l'application
            il y a moins de {{ staleness_days }} {{ staleness_days == 1 ? 'jour' : 'jours' }}.
        </p>
        {# Shown by offline-page.js only once it has found a recent copy of
           the home page: without one, « Accueil » brought back this very
           screen and looked like a button that did nothing. #}
        <p class="text-body-secondary small d-none" id="offline-nothing-saved">
            La page d'accueil n'est pas enregistrée sur cet appareil.
        </p>
        <div class="d-flex flex-column flex-sm-row gap-2 mt-2">
            <button type="button" id="offline-retry-btn" class="btn btn-primary">Réessayer</button>
            <button type="button" id="offline-back-btn" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Retour</button>
            <a href="/" id="offline-home-link" class="btn btn-outline-secondary d-none">Accueil</a>
        </div>
    </div>
    <script src="{{ asset('/assets/js/offline-page.js') }}"></script>
</body>
</html>
